This project builds on open standards and open-source work by others. It
does not vendor their code; the runtime dependencies are installed
separately (see requirements.txt) and remain under their own licenses.

Standards
  - RFC 9421  HTTP Message Signatures
  - RFC 9530  Digest Fields (Content-Digest)
  - RFC 8785  JSON Canonicalization Scheme (JCS)
  - Ed25519 (RFC 8032) signatures

Third-party software
  - ggwave, the data-over-sound codec that carries the native gibberlink
    audio channel. Copyright Georgi Gerganov, MIT License.
    https://github.com/ggerganov/ggwave
  - PyNaCl / libsodium, for Ed25519 signing and verification.
  - rfc8785, a Python implementation of the JSON Canonicalization Scheme.
  - pqcrypto, post-quantum signature primitives used by the anchored demos.

Concept
  - "GibberLink" refers to the idea of two AI agents dropping from spoken
    language to an efficient data-over-sound protocol once they recognise
    each other as agents. This project implements a signed, verifiable
    variant of that idea; it is an independent implementation and is not
    affiliated with or endorsed by the authors of the original demo.
